TRADE MARKS ACT 1994
NOTIFICATION TO THE PROPRIETOR OF AN EARLIER TRADE MARK

We are writing to you because you are recorded as the proprietor of an
earlier trade mark which was identified during the examination of a later
trade mark application. That application has now been published in the Trade
Marks Journal.

This notification is sent for your information only. It does not mean that
the Office considers the marks to be in conflict, and no action is required
of you unless you choose to take it.

YOUR EARLIER TRADE MARK

    Trade mark:        ASOS
    Number:            UK00002530115
    Filing date:       28 October 2009
    Proprietor:        ASOS plc

PUBLISHED APPLICATION

    Trade mark:        Assos
    Number:            UK00004437218
    Applicant:         Meridian Velo Limited
    Filing date:       12 May 2026
    Date published:    26 June 2026
    Classes:           18, 25

    Class 18: Bags; handbags; shoulder bags; rucksacks; holdalls; wallets;
    purses; luggage; articles made of leather and imitations of leather.

    Class 25: Clothing; footwear; headgear; jackets; trousers; shirts;
    knitwear; outerwear.

OPPOSITION

If you wish to oppose the registration of this application you must file a
notice of opposition on form TM7, together with the prescribed fee, before
the end of the opposition period.

    Opposition period ends:  26 August 2026

The opposition period is two months from the date of publication. It may be
extended to three months by filing form TM7A before the end of the initial
two month period. Form TM7A attracts no fee. If no opposition is filed and
no extension is requested, the application will proceed to registration.

You may also wish to consider whether the matter can be resolved directly
with the applicant. The Office cannot advise you on the merits of any
opposition or provide legal advice.

Further information about opposition proceedings is available at
www.gov.uk/guidance/opposing-a-trade-mark-application.

